{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nCurrent `origin/main` already contains the bug-2f46 core decoupling: `run_http_with_grace` drives certified-op drain through `InFlightGauge`/`drain_then_exit` and gives uvicorn a separate short graceful-shutdown timeout. This ticket closes the approved 2026-09-01 DECISION by making that separation explicit and durable for the parentless 40a7 bug: name the uvicorn timer as a transport backstop, set its concrete default to 30 seconds, preserve compatibility for existing callers, and add direct tests for the two shutdown directions the incident requires.\n\nThe certified-op drain grace remains `DEFAULT_SHUTDOWN_GRACE_SECONDS = 1200`. That value is the primary drain deadline for in-flight certified ops and is enforced by `drain_then_exit`; it is not uvicorn's `timeout_graceful_shutdown`.\n\nDeadline-elapse disposition: if the certified-op drain deadline expires while the gauge is still busy, the retiring process sets `server.should_exit`; uvicorn begins graceful shutdown and the in-flight client receives the terminal shutdown/connection disposition from the transport. That is distinct from the idle path, where `should_exit` is set only after the gauge is already idle and uvicorn's short backstop sweeps idle held-open streams.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_mcp_health.py` exports `DEFAULT_UVICORN_BACKSTOP_SECONDS = 30` as the named uvicorn transport backstop.\n- [ ] Existing imports of `DEFAULT_UVICORN_GRACEFUL_SECONDS` remain compatible as an alias for the new backstop constant.\n- [ ] `run_http_with_grace` passes uvicorn `timeout_graceful_shutdown=int(uvicorn_backstop_seconds)` instead of using the certified-op `grace_seconds` value.\n- [ ] `run_http_with_grace` preserves the existing keyword `uvicorn_graceful_seconds` as a backward-compatible override for callers while documenting `uvicorn_backstop_seconds` as the preferred name.\n- [ ] `drain_then_exit` still uses `grace_seconds` as the certified-op drain deadline.\n- [ ] The SIGTERM handler calls `gauge.begin_draining()` immediately when retirement starts.\n- [ ] The SIGTERM handler sets `server.should_exit` only after the gauge is idle or the certified-op drain deadline elapses.\n- [ ] An idle-gauge retirement test proves `server.should_exit` is set immediately/quickly with `grace_seconds=1200`, demonstrating the early-exit path is well under the certified-op grace.\n- [ ] A busy-gauge retirement test injects a small `grace_seconds` and a shorter uvicorn backstop value and proves `server.should_exit` is not set until the gauge drains or the injected certified-op deadline elapses, so the short uvicorn backstop does not cut short an in-flight certified op.\n- [ ] The change is self-contained in in-process MCP shutdown logic and does not depend on any CI provider or deployment-specific external service.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Focused: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_http_transport.py -k \"mcp_retirement or run_http_with_grace or drain_then_exit or sigterm\"`\n- Lint: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- Typecheck: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make typecheck`\n- Gerrit: land only after `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, and no unresolved comments.","title":"mcp retirement should codify a short uvicorn backstop separate from certified-op drain grace"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788290568555900518,"uuid":"5c6d9743-2da0-4311-8e88-4a8b81f03e1f"}